WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:01.370
Okay.

00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:02.370
Next question.

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:03.370
David.

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:08.420
Should Democrats either slow down or speed
up the impeachment process?

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:14.139
Listen, I think that the timing of impeachment
is just fine and I think that there are bigger

00:00:14.139 --> 00:00:18.560
issues about the impeachment and whether it's
going to be politically effective, which for

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:19.870
me is the main consideration.

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:24.810
I still am on the side of impeachment is not
going to remove Donald Trump.

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:25.810
Okay.

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:30.620
Every time I say it, some people email me,
they say, David, you're putting the cart before

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:35.239
the horse or you conceding a loss already
on.

00:00:35.239 --> 00:00:37.699
It's possible that impeachment could remove
Donald Trump.

00:00:37.699 --> 00:00:39.559
I see it as extraordinarily unlikely.

00:00:39.559 --> 00:00:44.679
I see the potential benefits, the political
ones that will damage Trump in the 2020 reelection

00:00:44.679 --> 00:00:51.109
campaign that he is very quickly ramping up
so on that basis we've got a slow build going

00:00:51.109 --> 00:00:52.289
on right now.

00:00:52.289 --> 00:00:57.960
Even with just you know Trump demands due
process and tweets like crazy and then Democrats

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:02.829
put out a proposal and approve it to grant
him due process by officializing and codified

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:06.740
the inquiry and Trump goes crazy again for
some other reason.

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:11.040
Trump is panicking more and more every week
on Twitter which is what you want.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:13.030
You don't want to just drop everything at
once.

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:19.490
You want to consume Donald Trump from now
until November of 2020 with having to, as

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:25.830
he sees it, fight the impeachment on Twitter
and in the media all the time he spends doing

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:26.830
that is time.

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:29.050
He is not spent just campaigning on issues.

00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:31.840
Not that he's much of an issue based guy to
begin with.

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:33.280
It will be a continued build.

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:36.620
He will be tweeting nonsense daily, which
he has been.

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:41.220
Uh, when we get to the public hearings, I
would want to get to the public hearings in

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:47.070
the next month or so and then go full speed
ahead as the democratic primaries get going

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:55.180
in February and onward in 2020 and just continue,
uh, putting in people's mind, not minds, not

00:01:55.180 --> 00:02:00.760
only what Donald Trump has done, but continuing
to push him to act in wackier and wackier

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:01.760
ways.

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:02.760
I think that that's all great.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:07.150
I'm fine also with making the timing politically
advantageous because I believe that the benefit

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:10.159
to be had from the impeachment inquiry is
a political benefit.

00:02:10.159 --> 00:02:12.159
I don't think it's actually the removal of
Trump.

00:02:12.159 --> 00:02:15.730
I know some people will email me and say,
here's how it could lead to Trump's removal.

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:21.530
I think it is extremely unlikely, so I'm fine
timing it to be damaging politically.

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:28.829
But ultimately what could completely backfire
is if Republicans, if Trumpists if Trump and

00:02:28.829 --> 00:02:35.280
the people around him are able to just ignore
the subpoenas successfully and already we

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:38.329
learned this week, a whole bunch of people
who were supposed to show up on Monday simply

00:02:38.329 --> 00:02:39.719
weren't showing up.

00:02:39.719 --> 00:02:45.310
If they're able to get away with that, they
will successfully weave a counter narrative

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:50.659
that actually could backfire on Democrats
for 2020.

00:02:50.659 --> 00:02:52.519
It could make Democrats appear weak.

00:02:52.519 --> 00:02:56.260
They couldn't even get people to show up and
the entire thing was bogus anyway.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:58.749
So the question for me is not the timing.

00:02:58.749 --> 00:03:00.580
I think the trajectory is fine.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:05.390
I think for all of her, her faults, Nancy
Pelosi actually has a pretty good sense of

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:09.849
what the timing should be to build as the
democratic primary and eventually the general

00:03:09.849 --> 00:03:11.000
election get going.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:17.700
I think the make or break is going to be do
Democrats just appear to be totally a weak

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:25.829
flacid, uh, of failures when it comes to actually
getting people to provide documents and show

00:03:25.829 --> 00:03:27.120
up because that's what you need.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:30.769
You need the public hearings, you need the
documents and you need the news that will

00:03:30.769 --> 00:03:35.090
build around that already there are question
marks as to whether Democrats are going to

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:40.340
be able to successfully do that question Mark
that hopefully will at some point be answered.

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:45.319
Let me know what you think about the trajectory
of the impeachment inquiry so far.

00:03:45.319 --> 00:03:47.169
I think that the timing has been pretty much
spot on.

